doesn't, that probably means the plugin wasn't able to read the local=20
dictionary file correctly (for some reason), so I could go through my copy=
=20
and see if there's something problematic (but which didn't cause a problem=
=20
when I installed it on my browser).

- If "Browse Lojban Popup Dictionary" does bring up the dictionary browser,=
=20
but none of your searches bring up any results, it could be a similar=20
problem to the previous.


